'''Dice Rooms'''  are [[special room]]s that can randomize many elements of the run. Dice Rooms require two {{e|Key}}s to be opened, unlike most other special rooms. For a Dice Room to spawn,  two things must happen;
* First, the game must decide that a {{R|Sacrifice Room}} will spawn that floor. This normally has a 1/7 (~14%) chance of happening each floor, but increases to 5/14 (~36%) if Isaac’s total health (filled [[Hearts|red and soul hearts]]) is equal to or greater than his total Red Heart  Containers (including Bone Hearts).
* Once the game determines a Sacrifice Room will spawn, a Dice Room has a 1/50 (2%) chance to replace it. [[Level Generation|This chance increases to 27/125 (~22%) if Isaac has two or more keys.]]

== Effects ==
[[file:Dice room example.png|250px]]

In addition to whatever else the room holds, there will always be a symbol of one of the sides of a six-sided die in the 5x5 center of the room. The amount of pips shown will be between one to six, chosen randomly. When Isaac crosses the die, a certain effect will occur that randomizes a certain aspect of the run, dependent on how many pips were on the die face shown. Any given Dice Room can only give this effect once.

The die numbers and effects are:
* ⚀ 1 pip - {{dlc|na+}} Rerolls Isaac's currently held [[collectible]]s into items from the {{ip|Treasure Room|text=Treasure Room item pool}}, like the {{i|D4}} would. Activated collectibles can be changed into passive ones, but passive collectibles cannot turn into activated ones.
** {{dlc|a+}} Rerolls each of Isaac's passive items into a random item from the pool of the room where it was acquired.
** {{dlc|r}} Rerolls both Isaac's active and passive items.
** {{dlc|r}} Only rerolls the items of the character that stepped onto the dice in co-op.
*** Meaning that {{C|Tainted Forgotten}} has to be thrown on the button in order to take effect.
* ⚁ 2 pips - Rerolls all [[pickup]]s in the room, like the {{i|D20}} would.
* ⚂ 3 pips - Rerolls all [[pickup]]s and [[trinket]]s on the entire floor. This includes {{r|Shop}} [[pickup]]s. Does not reroll pickups or trinkets in the {{R|Devil Room}}, {{R|Angel Room}}, {{R|Black Market}}, or {{R|Crawl Space}}.
** Pickups rerolled in shops by this effect have a chance to turn into items. If these are active items, they will have no charges when picked up.
* ⚃ 4 pips - Rerolls any [[item|item pedestals]] on the floor, like {{i|The D6}} would. Does not reroll item pedestals in the {{R|Devil Room}}, {{R|Angel Room}}, {{R|Library}}, {{R|Black Market}}, or {{R|Crawl Space}}.
* ⚄ 5 pips - Rerolls and restarts the current floor, which is the same effect as {{i|Forget Me Now}}.
* ⚅ 6 pips - Combines the effects of the 1-, 3-, and 4-pip rooms. (Rerolls all held items (including active), pickups, trinkets, and pedestal items like the {{i|D100}}.)
** {{dlc|r}} Rerolls all held items for all characters in co-op.

